.TH MDV 1 "July 2026" "mdv 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mdv \- full-screen terminal Markdown viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mdv
[\fIflags\fR] \fIfile.md\fR
.br
.B mdv
[\fIflags\fR] [\fIdirectory\fR]
.br
.B mdv
[\fIflags\fR] \fIfile.md\fR...
.br
.B mdv
[\fIflags\fR] \fIURL\fR
.br
.I command
|
.B mdv
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mdv
renders CommonMark + GFM Markdown full-screen in the terminal: syntax-highlighted
code, box-drawing tables, incremental search, a fuzzy table-of-contents jump,
link following with vimium-style hints and a jumplist, images (half-block mosaic
anywhere, kitty graphics in kitty/ghostty), LaTeX display math, live reload on
file change, and external editing at the current line.
.PP
Given a directory, or no argument at all, mdv lists the markdown files
underneath it and opens the one you pick. Type to filter the list, \fBenter\fR
opens, and \fBesc\fR leaves. Quitting a document returns to the list;
\fBctrl+c\fR leaves mdv outright. Dot directories and dependency trees
(\fInode_modules\fR, \fIvendor\fR, \fItarget\fR) are skipped. Naming several
files uses the same list, which makes it a buffer list.
.PP
An http or https URL is fetched, with a 20 second timeout and an 8 MiB cap.
\fIgithub.com/owner/repo\fR resolves to that repository's README, and a
\fIblob\fR link to the file it points at. One remote document is fetched at
a time, and relative links inside it do not resolve.
.PP
When standard output is not a terminal, the rendered document is written as
plain text instead.
.PP
Markdown piped on standard input leaves it used up, so the pager reads its
keys from the terminal directly. Where no terminal can supply them — a
sandbox, a CI runner, no controlling tty — mdv reports why and prints the
rendered document as plain text rather than failing, so a piped invocation
always produces output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-theme " name"
.BR default ,
.BR plain ,
or a path to a YAML theme file whose keys overlay the default theme.
.TP
.BI \-width " n"
Maximum content width in columns (default: terminal width, capped at 120).
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B j/k, d/u, space/b, g/G
Scroll: line, half page, page, top/bottom. The mouse wheel works too.
.TP
.B /
Incremental search (smart-case; enter keeps, esc cancels), then
.B n/N
between matches.
.TP
.B t
Table of contents; type to fuzzy-filter, enter jumps.
.TP
.B f
Link hints: type the overlaid label to follow. Clicking a link follows it as
well. Anchors and relative .md links open in mdv; other links go to the
desktop handler —
.BR xdg-open (1)
on Unix,
.BR open (1)
on macOS, rundll32 on Windows. Only http, https and mailto targets are
followed: a document is untrusted input, and other URI schemes hand it a
code-execution surface.
.TP
.B ctrl+o / tab
Jumplist back / forward, across documents.
.TP
.B e, i
Suspend and edit the file at the current line with \fB$EDITOR\fR (default vim).
The line is passed as \fB+N\fR, or in the form the editor expects:
\fB--goto\fR for the VS Code family, \fIfile:line\fR for subl and hx.
.TP
.B y
Copy the nearest code block to the clipboard (OSC 52).
.TP
.B ?, q
Help overlay; quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.MDView/config.yaml
Viewer settings (theme, width, editor, images, mermaid). Created with a
commented template on first run; command-line flags take precedence.
.IP
\fBmermaid\fR renders mermaid fences as diagrams through mermaid-cli
(\fBmmdc\fR on PATH) and is off by default: mmdc drives a headless browser
over content that came from the document. Off, missing, or failing to
compile, the fence stays a syntax-highlighted code block.
.TP
.I ~/.MDView/theme.yaml
User theme, overlaying the built-in adaptive theme key by key. Created as
a commented template on first run.
.TP
.I ~/.MDView/keys.yaml
User keymap. Listing keys for an action replaces that action's defaults
entirely; an empty list leaves it unbound. Unknown action names, and a key
claimed by two actions, are errors. \fBctrl+c\fR always quits. Created as a
commented template on first run.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor for the e/i binding (overridden by \fIconfig.yaml\fR's editor key).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables styling.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Reading positions persist under \fI$XDG_STATE_HOME/mdv/positions.json\fR
(default \fI~/.local/state/mdv/\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glow (1),
.BR less (1)
